<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-weight: bold; font-size: =
22px;">People really enjoy seeing what the average person eats in a day</sp=
an><br><br>You may recall the social media curmudgeons of yore who complain=
ed about seeing their friends=E2=80=99 lunches on Instagram. Well, they=E2=
=80=99re gonna hate TikTok.&nbsp;<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">People are eating up videos detailing everyth=
ing the poster consumes in a single day, often hashtagged =E2=80=9CWIEIAD=
=E2=80=9D (or =E2=80=9Cwhat I eat in a day=E2=80=9D).&nbsp;<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">It=E2=80=99s not a brand new trend and may se=
em even like an obvious content type for fitness or nutrition influencers. =
A May article in <span style=3D"font-style: italic;">PopSugar</span> <a hre=
f=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/MWy1YXd7BC2W7Vqj--7c=
YySnW1f4B6k5Hc4Z-N95jt8v2-ZW0W6N1vHY6lZ3nwW1MbJpz4YVRPMW6QGVk_1cYTKJW5YzXwv=
